## Figure caption

**Figure 1: Logit-shift distillation.** At position (t), the draft’s top-1 prediction (a_t) differs from the target’s preferred token ((\textit{puppy}) versus (\textit{dog})) but remains within the target’s top-(k), triggering a substitution. The original context (x_1,\ldots,x_t) and the substituted context (x_1,\ldots,x_{t-1},a_t) are processed by both models to obtain their distributions after position (t). The loss matches the draft’s centered logit shift (\Delta_D) to the target’s shift (\Delta_T), supervising how candidate continuations are re-ranked when the preceding token changes rather than matching the output at either context alone.
